---
title: Accipitriformes
---
# Accipitriformes

Accipitriformes is the order of diurnal birds of prey, taking in the hawks,
eagles, kites, harriers and the [[osprey]]. All have a hooked bill, powerful
feet with curved talons, and binocular vision far sharper than a human's. The
New World vultures are now placed here too, though the arrangement has been
moved more than once; the [[andean-condor]] is the largest of them. Most species
are solitary outside the breeding season and hold large territories.
